      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limits for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This could cause hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day).\n2. **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day), which is the standard maximum.\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another regimen you prefer.\n\nIf you really do want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
      }
